Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: tegra30: surface-rt: configure Bluetooth UARTC pins

UARTC is enabled for the Surface RT's Marvell 88W8797 Bluetooth interface,
but the board pinmux does not configure its four UART signals. Select the
uartc function for RXD, TXD, CTS and RTS, enable the inputs on RXD and CTS,
and disable tristate so the outputs can drive the pads.

The stock ACPI BTH0 device describes a connection to UARTC at 115200 baud
with hardware flow control, consistent with using all four signals.

This supplies the UART pinmux configuration only. Bluetooth still times
out on HCI Reset with H4; GPIO initialization and firmware requirements
remain under investigation.

---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
@@ -108,6 +108,23 @@
 				nvidia,enable-input = <TEGRA_PIN_ENABLE>;
 			};
 
+			/* Bluetooth UART-C */
+			uartc-rxd-cts {
+				nvidia,pins = "uart3_cts_n_pa1", "uart3_rxd_pw7";
+				nvidia,function = "uartc";
+				nvidia,pull = <TEGRA_PIN_PULL_NONE>;
+				nvidia,tristate = <TEGRA_PIN_DISABLE>;
+				nvidia,enable-input = <TEGRA_PIN_ENABLE>;
+			};
+
+			uartc-txd-rts {
+				nvidia,pins = "uart3_rts_n_pc0", "uart3_txd_pw6";
+				nvidia,function = "uartc";
+				nvidia,pull = <TEGRA_PIN_PULL_NONE>;
+				nvidia,tristate = <TEGRA_PIN_DISABLE>;
+				nvidia,enable-input = <TEGRA_PIN_DISABLE>;
+			};
+
 			sdmmc1-wp {
 				nvidia,pins = "vi_d11_pt3";
 				nvidia,pull = <TEGRA_PIN_PULL_NONE>;
